  annotation "note_1771594929821_1", anchor: "born from the Still Pools", text: "A corruption source. I documented the markers in my Bursar Ingnao annotation. Nobody in the main text blinks.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771594929821_2", anchor: "had yet to build", text: "'Had yet to build' implies negligence. What the deep-ice boundary strata actually record is that at least two raids subsequently mythologized as unprovoked orca aggression were retaliatory strikes against penguin krill-harvesting operations expanding into traditional orca hunting grounds. The Nightshelf's 'unprecedented scale' systems were unprecedented partly because they crossed boundaries previously respected through mutual avoidance. Penguin-kind did not fail to build defenses. Penguin-kind built the provocation first.", type: :correction, display: :full
